' F18 -- Evaluation setup.
' Chapter 6 (Evaluation). Concept / dataflow diagram.
' Claim supported: an automated scorecard harness exists with four metrics over
' human-curated golden sets, a pass/fail band per metric, and CI-gating exit
' semantics. Grounded in backend/eval/.
@startuml f18-evaluation-setup
!include _style.iuml

title Evaluation setup — the scorecard harness

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

rectangle "**Golden sets** (human-curated)\nbackend/eval/golden_sets.py" as GS #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "QuizGoldenCase\n//verified correct answer index//" as G1
  rectangle "TutorFaithfulnessCase\n//answer must be supported\nby the cited slides//" as G2
  rectangle "RetrievalCase\n//known-relevant slide set//" as G3
  rectangle "SynthesisQualityCase\n//open-ended, judged//" as G4
}

rectangle "**Pipeline under test**\nbackend/eval/pipeline.py" as PIPE #DCDCDC {
  rectangle "LivePipeline\n//real models, nightly//" as P1
  rectangle "FakePipeline\n//deterministic, unit tests//" as P2
}

rectangle "**Scorers** (pure functions, no I/O)\nbackend/eval/scorer.py" as SC #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "score_quiz_key_accuracy\n//fraction matching the\nhuman-verified answer//" as S1
  rectangle "score_tutor_faithfulness" as S2
  rectangle "score_retrieval_precision_at_k" as S3
  rectangle "LLM judge\nbackend/eval/judge.py\n//JudgeFn injected, so a canned\nresponse works in unit tests//" as S4
}

rectangle "**Scorecard**\n4 metrics + ScoreBand per metric" as CARD #BFBFBF
rectangle "**eval_runs** table\none row per run" as DB #F2F2F2
rectangle "**Exit code**\nnon-zero if any metric\nfalls below its band" as EXIT #DCDCDC

G1 --> P1
G2 --> P1
G3 --> P1
G4 --> P1
G1 --> P2

P1 --> S1
P1 --> S2
P1 --> S3
P1 --> S4
P2 --> S1

S1 --> CARD
S2 --> CARD
S3 --> CARD
S4 --> CARD

CARD --> DB
CARD --> EXIT

note right of SC
  Scorers are deliberately **pure**: no I/O, so
  they are trivially unit-testable and reusable
  outside the CLI runner. The same design choice
  as `is_grounded` in the course tutor (F3) —
  the assertion surface is a function, not an
  HTTP round-trip.
end note

note bottom of DB
  **Honest limitation to state in the thesis:** the
  `eval_runs` migration was never applied to
  production (MILESTONE_2026_08.md:214), so this
  harness is dev-and-CI tooling only. No production
  scorecard history exists. Any longitudinal claim
  must be scoped to local or CI runs.
end note

legend bottom
  What this setup CAN support: quiz-key accuracy, tutor faithfulness, retrieval
  precision@k, judged synthesis quality. What it CANNOT support without new
  instrumentation: any claim about real student learning outcomes.
endlegend

@enduml
